rules_version = '2';

// Photographs of the people PRAVDA books. Every one of them is personal data,
// and whether a given photo may be seen by a given reader depends on a consent
// record that lives in Firestore and on the reader's identity — a decision
// these rules cannot make, and must never be asked to.
//
// So, like firestore.rules, this file's whole job is to deny the client SDK
// outright. Photos are written and read only by route handlers using the Admin
// SDK, which bypasses these rules, and each read is checked against the
// person's live consent first (lib/talent/photo.ts). A public bucket URL would
// outlive a withdrawn consent in every cache it reached.
//
// If a rule here ever needs loosening, that is the signal that a photo is
// about to be served without anyone checking whether its subject agreed.
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    match /{allPaths=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
